1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,133
A wallet shows what moved, not why.

2
00:00:04,133 --> 00:00:10,000
RecallLedger demonstrates how an assistant
can remember a correction without

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,700
assuming every similar transfer means the
same thing.

4
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:20,000
This walkthrough uses synthetic teaching
data, not customer payments.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,867
In this local sandbox, I label one
transfer as tools.

6
00:00:25,867 --> 00:00:31,767
Reusing that label needs a separate
confirmation of recipient, asset,

7
00:00:31,767 --> 00:00:34,700
direction, amount range and validity.

8
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:40,000
While the fixture job is pending, policy
stays unchanged.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,867
Complete fixture job is a simulation, not
a Walrus receipt.

10
00:00:45,867 --> 00:00:50,600
I then correct a twenty-five-unit transfer
to reimbursement.

11
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:53,533
That changes this item only.

12
00:00:53,533 --> 00:00:57,633
Narrowing future matches from
five-through-thirty to five-through-twenty

13
00:00:57,633 --> 00:01:00,000
requires another explicit confirmation.

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,667
Here are memory off and on for the same
twelve-unit input, at

15
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:08,900
the same evaluation time.

16
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:11,100
The input hashes match.

17
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:17,233
Without context it asks; with the
confirmed rule it becomes tools.

18
00:01:17,233 --> 00:01:21,100
After narrowing, the twenty-five-unit
input asks again.

19
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:26,667
An incoming transfer cannot inherit an
outgoing label: a refund

20
00:01:26,667 --> 00:01:28,900
needs an explicit link.

21
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:32,233
After revocation, future matches ask
again.

22
00:01:32,233 --> 00:01:37,767
This demonstrates deterministic policy
replay, not model training or measured

23
00:01:37,767 --> 00:01:40,000
improvement on real users.

24
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,800
These are recorded evidence files, not a
new write.

25
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:49,067
WP6a stored twelve synthetic teaching
memories, M01 through

26
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:51,200
M12, on Walrus Mainnet.

27
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:56,000
Reconciliation shows twelve done
operations and no unresolved operations.

28
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:02,400
The verified manifest reports count
twelve, exact set true and hashes true.

29
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:06,667
Each entry supplies its event and text
hashes.

30
00:02:06,667 --> 00:02:10,933
Storage is real; the business story is
synthetic.

31
00:02:10,933 --> 00:02:17,867
One recorded Tatum read succeeded, but the
real-transfer loop was not run by

32
00:02:17,867 --> 00:02:20,000
owner decision one B.

33
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,100
The recorded fresh-client restore reports
verified, with the same manifest

34
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:28,167
version, count twelve and state hash.

35
00:02:28,167 --> 00:02:33,267
The full hash and original check time are
on screen.

36
00:02:33,267 --> 00:02:38,367
The demo cannot write; Mainnet writes
belong only to the

37
00:02:38,367 --> 00:02:40,400
separately authorized operator host.

38
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:45,000
These are recorded results, not a current
availability guarantee.
